# VTID-03946 — commands actually run.

# --- Investigation ---------------------------------------------------------

# User showed a real Operator Console conversation: asked Operator to scope
# a frontend change, and Operator replied "I don't yet see where the actual
# console UI lives" — asking 8 clarifying questions (repo path, framework,
# etc.) instead of just finding the answer, after running dev_search_codebase
# for "Operator Console" and getting zero frontend hits.

grep -n "dev_search_codebase" -A 40 services/gateway/src/services/gemini-operator.ts
#   -> tool description: "Search the exafyltd/vitana-platform codebase..."
#      hardcoded single-repo, GitHub Search Code API-backed.

grep -n "function searchCode" -A 20 services/gateway/src/services/github-service.ts
#   -> confirmed: a thin wrapper around GET /search/code, no size-limit
#      handling of its own.

wc -c services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js
#   -> 2,564,394 bytes (~2.5MB). GitHub's Search Code API documented limit:
#      files over 384KB are excluded from the index entirely.

# Reproduced the EXACT live failure via the real GitHub Search Code API
# (mcp__github__search_code, same underlying endpoint dev_search_codebase
# calls):
#   query: repo:exafyltd/vitana-platform Operator Console
#   -> 263 total hits across the repo (operator-service.ts, operator.ts,
#      operator-planner.ts, many docs/validation/*.md files, etc.)
#   -> ZERO hits from services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js,
#      even though that file contains the literal string 'Operator Console'
#      (renderOperatorOverlay(): title.textContent = 'Operator Console';).
#   This proves the 384KB exclusion, not a query-wording problem — no
#   query could ever surface content inside that file via this tool.

# Second, independent, more consequential cause (raised directly by the
# user): dev_search_codebase/dev_read_file are hardcoded to
# OPERATOR_DEFAULT_REPO ('exafyltd/vitana-platform') with literally no way
# to reach exafyltd/vitana-v1 — the separate repo holding the actual
# consumer-facing Vitana app frontend (this repo's own frontend is only the
# internal Command Hub admin console). Confirmed via the tool's own
# parameter schema: no "repo" field existed at all.

grep -n "FRONTEND_DEPLOY_TOKEN\|FRONTEND_DEPLOY_REPO" services/gateway/src/
#   -> found an ALREADY-PROVISIONED cross-repo credential
#      (services/gateway/src/routes/operator.ts, PUBLISH-button frontend
#      promotion) scoped to exafyltd/vitana-v1 — reused here rather than
#      requesting/wiring a new credential (CLAUDE.md ALWAYS rule 9: prefer
#      existing systems over rebuilding).

# --- Fix ---------------------------------------------------------------

# services/gateway/src/services/gemini-operator.ts
#   1. dev_search_codebase / dev_read_file gained an optional, allowlisted
#      "repo" parameter (exafyltd/vitana-platform default, or
#      exafyltd/vitana-v1) — resolveOperatorRepo() rejects anything else
#      outright, and resolves the vitana-v1 token lazily via
#      operatorRepoToken() (reads process.env.FRONTEND_DEPLOY_TOKEN at CALL
#      time, not module-load time, so a task-def env change takes effect
#      without a restart — same convention as BEDROCK_ROLE_ARN, CLAUDE.md
#      §2b). Fails loudly (repo_token_not_configured) rather than silently
#      falling back to the wrong token when FRONTEND_DEPLOY_TOKEN is unset.
#   2. Both tool descriptions and CODEBASE_OVERVIEW_BLOCK (the always-on
#      orientation block, VTID-03930) now explicitly state: two repos exist,
#      most frontend/UI code is in vitana-v1 not vitana-platform, and
#      dev_search_codebase always returns zero hits inside app.js
#      specifically (384KB GitHub index exclusion) — use dev_read_file with
#      an explicit path there instead.
#   3. Default-repo call shape is UNCHANGED (still exactly 3 positional args
#      to searchCode/getFileContents) so VTID-03835's own pre-existing tests
#      needed no changes — verified by running them unmodified.

node --check services/gateway/src/services/gemini-operator.ts 2>&1 || true
#   (TypeScript file — real check is tsc below, this just confirms no stray
#   syntax typo before running the type checker)

# --- Verification -----------------------------------------------------------

cd services/gateway

npx jest test/vtid-03835-operator-console-read-tools.test.ts --runInBand
#   -> 20/20 tests pass UNCHANGED — confirms the default-repo path is
#      byte-for-byte backward compatible. (outputs/targeted-tests.txt)

npx jest test/vtid-03946-operator-cross-repo-search.test.ts --runInBand
#   -> 8/8 new tests pass. (outputs/targeted-tests.txt)

# Mutation check: git stash'd gemini-operator.ts (reverting the fix), re-ran
# the new test file -- confirmed 6/8 tests fail (the 2 default-repo-path
# tests still pass since they don't exercise the new behavior at all).
# git stash pop restored the fix -- 8/8 green again.

npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> 2 pre-existing, unrelated errors only (missing @aws-sdk sub-packages
#      in this session's local node_modules — declared in package.json, not
#      referenced by any file this VTID touches). Zero errors in
#      gemini-operator.ts or the new test file. (outputs/tsc.txt)

npx jest --runInBand
#   -> full suite, run in background; see outputs/full-suite.txt for the
#      final tally. Same pre-existing failing-suite set as every other
#      evidence pack in this session (missing @aws-sdk sub-packages),
#      confirmed unrelated to this VTID.
